WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, one of the things
we've seen happen,

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:04.637
sort of the last month or so,
is Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:09.209 align:start size:94% position:6%
has proposed this
70% marginal tax rate.

00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:11.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, you know, and then,
you know, people --

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:13.513
So it's the money you make
over $10 million gets taxed.

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:16.082 size:81% position:41%
-Yeah, you get to have
your first $10 million

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:17.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
taxed like normal people.
-Yeah.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
-After that, you got to pay
a little more.

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:24.758
And 70% of the country says now,
in a Fox News poll, by the way,

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:30.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they support her plan
to tax at the 70% rate

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:30.830 size:84% position:42% line:92%
those over $10 million.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:32.332 size:81% position:41%
-And what do you think
that shift has been?

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:34.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause I don't think it would
have been 70%

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:35.301 size:75% position:38% line:92%
even five years ago.

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:36.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it the stories you were
just talking about?

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:38.838
Is it that people see their
infrastructures crumbling

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:41.074
and people are also buying homes
for $200-plus-million?

00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:43.810
-It's all of that, but it's also
that people realize

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:45.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
that this myth that we were
raised on,

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:49.215
the Horatio Alger story that
anybody can make it in America.

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:50.450 line:92%
Anybody could be a millionaire.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
Anybody could be president of
the United States.

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:56.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, we already --
well, we know that one's true.

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:58.058 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:58.058 --> 00:01:00.727
-Yeah, that one -- that's
definitely true now, yeah.

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:02.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I think people
now know that, no,

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:05.732
because everybody is living
from paycheck to paycheck.

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:08.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
Half of the country does not
have enough money

00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:11.271
in their bank account tonight
if a loved one passed away,

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:14.274
they don't have the money to fly
across the country

00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:14.974 size:78% position:39% line:92%
to go to the funeral.

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:20.146
The majority of Americans have
$400 or less available to them.

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:22.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
That is -- That's the majority
of our country.

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:26.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
So if they have an emergency
or something happens,

00:01:26.019 --> 00:01:27.320 size:84% position:42% line:92%
people can't afford it.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:28.288 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That has to change.

00:01:28.288 --> 00:01:29.289 line:92%
And I'll tell you, the rich,

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:31.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
the Howard Schultzes
and the Michael Bloombergs,

00:01:31.825 --> 00:01:34.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
they better get a clue
because they are tone deaf

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:36.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the fact
that people have had it.

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:38.865
And I think people -- that's why
they support taxing the rich.

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:43.503
They support -- They see other
countries have free healthcare

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:46.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we are still paying
through the nose

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:49.209 align:start size:94% position:6%
and going through
all this rigmarole.

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:49.776 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
This has to stop.

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:53.780
And I hope -- Look, we've got
good candidates who are running.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:56.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
Some of them are running
on this, you know.

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:58.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would also add, again,
if I were running --

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:01.354
And I'm saying if 'cause I heard
the other night,

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:04.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
you said on the air
no one has announced.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:04.624 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right.

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:05.425 line:92%
-I'm not announcing tonight.

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:08.528
-Thank you. I would love you
to save that for another show.

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:09.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you.
-Yes.

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:12.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it should happen here.
-Yeah, thank you.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:14.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just out of courtesy to you.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:17.070
And a vast appreciation that
the American public has for you

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:19.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
and what you do every night
on this show.

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:20.607 line:92%
-Very kind of you. Thank you.

00:02:20.607 --> 00:02:21.341 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-So thank you for that.

00:02:21.341 --> 00:02:22.942 size:84% position:42%
No, no, no. It's true.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:28.481
But I would -- Yesterday, they
reported the U.S. Postal Service

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:30.250 line:92%
lost $4 billion last year.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:33.419
They're talking about
eliminating the postal service.

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:36.523
No, if I were president, I would
keep the postal service.

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:40.193
I would give the mailwomen
and mailmen a job every --

00:02:40.193 --> 00:02:40.994 size:81% position:41% line:92%
at least every Friday,

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:44.230
they would deliver two joints
to every mailbox in America.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:48.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Compliments of
your federal government.

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:49.369 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:49.369 --> 00:02:52.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you know -- and just two.
We're not talking just --

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:53.173 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right.

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:56.109
-Country won't work if everybody
is completely stoned.

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:56.676 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But just two.

00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:59.345
And it gives the postal service
a job.

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:01.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would try to think of things
like that to do.

00:03:01.781 --> 00:03:02.782 line:92%
-I think that's a good platform.

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:04.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to talk --
Last time you were here

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:06.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
was right before the midterms.
-Yes.

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:09.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I'll admit,
there was a little pessimism.

00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:10.089 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:12.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You were fairly critical of
Nancy Pelosi,

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:15.261
particularly her optimism
going into the midterms.

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:17.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
So not only was her optimism
borne out,

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:19.666 line:92%
but how do you feel about her

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:22.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the handling
of the shutdown?

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:25.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I feel the same way
everybody feels.

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:29.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
She kicked his ass.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:29.075 --> 00:03:32.579 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was amazing.

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:36.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, many of us --
what is she, 78?

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:39.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
Many of us have had
a 78-year-old grandmother.

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:42.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you have one
that's really feisty

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:46.593
and really that puts her [bleep]
kicking boots on...

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:47.126 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:50.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't know
if I can say that, but...

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:55.935
No, listen, she -- I was very
skeptical, as I am of anybody,

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:59.172
any politician, anybody
in a leadership position.

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:02.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
But since the election,
she has --

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:03.476 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I mean, look what she --

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:07.013
she put Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez
and Rashida Tlaib,

00:04:07.013 --> 00:04:11.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
our first Palestinian-American
in Congress, from Detroit.

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:15.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
She put them on the government
oversight committee

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:18.992
that's going to be one of
the impeachment committees.

00:04:18.992 --> 00:04:19.425 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:21.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She put them on
the impeachment committees.

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:23.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's -- I thought,
"Wow, okay."

00:04:23.496 --> 00:04:26.399 size:81% position:41%
She got the message of
the November election.

00:04:26.399 --> 00:04:28.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's doing what
she should be doing.

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:30.136 line:92%
I think it's very powerful.

00:04:30.136 --> 00:04:32.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
The thing with Rashida, too,
to put her on --

00:04:32.338 --> 00:04:34.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
Remember on election night,
she went to that party

00:04:34.674 --> 00:04:37.710
and somebody filmed her with an
iPhone saying, you know...

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:40.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Go for it. Just tell them
in case they missed it.

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:42.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She just went up to
the microphone and says,

00:04:42.615 --> 00:04:44.851 size:75% position:38%
"We're gonna impeach
the mother[bleep]"

00:04:44.851 --> 00:04:47.820 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:50.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
And everybody --
everybody was like,

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:52.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, my gosh,
why did she say that?

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:55.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now she won't get
put on any committees."

00:04:55.595 --> 00:04:56.896 line:92%
And then what does Pelosi do?

00:04:56.896 --> 00:04:58.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
She puts her on
the impeachment committee.

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:00.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:00.867 --> 00:05:02.568 line:92%
-Oh! I'm not dreaming, right?

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:04.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
-I'm awake. I'm with you.

00:05:04.337 --> 00:05:07.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There's a lot
to keep our eye on, obviously,

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:10.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the coming months,
and please come back soon.

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:13.379
It's always just such a pleasure
to have you.

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:15.048 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Thank you very much.

